From 1004cc13c5ec06555ec22f3f689c13ef39fcb4d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: howl <howeili@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 10:19:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm89: the window KV in V4.1's own layout (SGLANG_SM89_V41_KV)

The checkpoint stores its window KV as all 512 values, RoPE part included, in e4m3 with a
UE8M0 scale per 32, after rounding to bf16 after the norm and after RoPE (_window_kv in
model.py); SGLang's V41 layout (528 B a token) and its writer do the same. SM89 kept the
V4 layout on all 40 layers: 448 values per 64-value scale, the RoPE part in bf16.

With SGLANG_SM89_V41_KV=1, on compute capability 8.9 only (it implies
SGLANG_SM89_FP4_COMPRESSED_KV):
- select_dsv4_kv_layout gives V41, so the ratio-1/2 caches are V41_FP4; another GPU, or a
  conflicting SGLANG_DSV4_KV_LAYOUT / SGLANG_DSV4_COMPRESSED_KV_LAYOUT, refuses to start;
- the dual-scope decode kernels, unsplit and split-K, read the 528-byte main rows through
  sm89_v41_tile.v41_tile in a copy of _process_kv_block_aggressive (MAIN_V41, a
  constexpr). e4m3 x a power of two is exact in bf16.
The V41 store floors its scale at 2^-13 where the checkpoint floors at 2^-22; the fix is
sgl-project/sglang#48500 and not part of this patch. Only blocks whose largest value is
under 0.0448 can differ.

Checked by howl9003 on an RTX 4080 SUPER, on their SM89 build (SGLang 5d8e90a0, the
unsplit kernel, the scale floor fixed):
- the store against act_quant (block 32, UE8M0): 0 of 151,011,328 values differ;
- the reader against the dequantization: 0 of 4,521,984; the attention against a bf16-row
  twin: 0 of 3,000 calls; off, against the files before: 0 of 600 calls; no spills;
- with FP4 compressed KV and FP32 logits, panel KL against the reference 0.01106 -> 0.01019
  (the reference's own noise floor 0.00996), top-1 96.74% -> 96.98%, NLL paired by
  conversation -0.00034 (SE 0.00069); the 24 tools/nll.py pieces +0.0025 (SE 0.0036);
  decode, median of six workloads, 32.98 -> 33.3 tok/s; 35K prefill +0.6%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
